* Add more filesystem options to mkfs.briefs as they become available.
* Make man pages.
* The codebase is starting to feel a bit hairy. It could stand another round of
  refactoring.
* The FUSE bridge is read-only right now. It should be read-write.
* [Done for xfstests] mkfs.briefs and fsck.briefs command line flags are
  sufficiently xfstests-compatible (force flag `-f`, check-only default,
  `-r -y` repair shape). Further standards alignment may be useful.
* [Done] fsck.briefs validates inode extended-attribute chains (magic, header
  version, used_size, CRC32C, entry bounds, continuation blocks, chain length
  and loop detection) and records xattr blocks in the allocator cross-reference.
* [Done] Keep the Go `Inode` struct in sync with the kernel on-disk inode
  layout. The `user_flags` field (carved from reserved padding) is now mirrored
  in `briefs/inode.go` and `gen_disk.go` so mkfs/fsck agree with the driver on
  inode size and field placement.
